                <pb facs="0711" n="611" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg611"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.01/228: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Davis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-08-12T17:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 12,
                                1920—5 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 12:50
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>1218. Greatest perplexity exists in official circles here regarding French
                    recognition of Wrangel. General idea appears that France has taken independent
                    action. No official statement yet forthcoming; House adjourned until Monday.
                    Paris informed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Davis</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
